# Database Design Rules

> **MANDATORY:** Read `.cursor/skills/database-change/SKILL.md` before ANY database work.
> Complete `.cursor/architecture/DATABASE-CHANGE-CHECKLIST.md` before and after every change.
> Update `database-blueprint.md` after every schema change — no exceptions.

Reference: `.cursor/architecture/database-blueprint.md`

## Migration Naming
```
YYYY_MM_DD_HHMMSS_create_{schema}_{table}_table.php
```

## Every Transactional Table Must Have
```php
$table->id(); // BIGINT
$table->timestamps(); // created_at, updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ
// Plus effective_from/effective_to for temporal entities
```

## Foreign Keys
Always define FK constraints with explicit onDelete behavior:
```php
$table->foreignId('student_id')->constrained('students.students')->restrictOnDelete();
$table->foreignId('academic_year_id')->constrained('academic.academic_years')->restrictOnDelete();
```

## Constraints in DB, Not Just App
```php
$table->decimal('grade', 5, 2);
$table->check('grade >= 0 AND grade <= 100');
$table->unique(['student_id', 'academic_year_id']); // where appropriate
```

## Index FK Columns Used in Queries
```php
$table->index(['school_id', 'academic_year_id']);
$table->index(['student_id', 'attendance_date']);
```

## PostgreSQL Schemas
Use PostgreSQL schemas matching domains: `organization`, `academic`, `students`, `enrollment`, etc.

## Never
- Use TINYINT (use smallInteger)
- Skip FK constraints "for performance"
- Store files in DB (metadata only; files in object storage)
- Delete academic history rows
